source: https://drveganblog.com/pan-fried-garlic-focaccia/
yield: 8 pieces
notes: |
  No oven needed — it's cooked covered in a pan on the stovetop, which is the whole point
  of the recipe.

  Prep 4 hrs 20 mins, cook 15 mins, rise 1 day, total 1 day 35 mins.

  480ml water to 625g flour is 77% hydration, so expect a slack, sticky dough — that's
  correct, don't flour it into submission. It's shaped loose and never kneaded after the
  rise.

  Written vegan. Dairy butter and real parmesan swap in at the same weights if you're not
  fussed.
components:
  - name: dough
    ingredients:
      - item: active dry yeast
        qty: 2.25
        unit: tsp
        note: 2 1/4 tsp
      - item: lukewarm water
        mass: 480
        qty: 480
        unit: ml
      - item: all-purpose flour
        mass: 625
        basis: true
      - item: salt
        qty: 2.5
        unit: tsp
      - item: extra-virgin olive oil
        qty: 4
        unit: tbsp
    steps:
      - in a large bowl, mix the lukewarm water and yeast and let sit for 5 mins until lightly foamy
      - add the flour and salt and mix until no dry flour remains
      - add the olive oil and mix until incorporated; the dough should be soft and slightly sticky
  - name: first rise
    steps:
      - transfer the dough to a lightly oiled bowl, cover, and refrigerate 8-24 hrs until doubled in size and bubbly
      - alternatively, let rise at room temperature for 3-4 hrs
  - name: shape
    steps:
      - divide the dough into two equal portions and gently shape each into loose rounds without kneading
  - name: pan-fry
    ingredients:
      - item: extra-virgin olive oil
        note: for the pan, a generous amount
    steps:
      - heat two pans over medium-low heat and add a generous amount of olive oil
      - once the oil is hot and shimmering, carefully place the dough into the pans
      - cover and cook 6-8 mins until the bottom is golden and crisp
      - flip carefully, add more olive oil if needed, cover again, and cook 5-7 mins until cooked through
  - name: garlic butter topping
    ingredients:
      - item: olive oil
        qty: 240
        unit: ml
      - item: garlic
        qty: 8
        unit: clove
        note: 8-10, peeled
      - item: vegan butter
        mass: 60
        note: softened
      - item: vegan parmesan
        mass: 50
        note: finely grated
      - item: fresh parsley
        qty: 2
        unit: tbsp
        note: 2-3 tbsp, finely chopped
      - item: salt
        note: to taste
      - item: black pepper
        note: to taste
      - item: chili flakes
        optional: true
    steps:
      - add the garlic cloves and olive oil to a small saucepan
      - cook over very low heat for 20-25 mins until the garlic is soft and lightly golden
      - mash the garlic with a small amount of the oil and mix with vegan butter until smooth
      - stir in vegan parmesan, parsley, salt, pepper, and chili flakes
